    <briefdescription>
<para>Move-only RAII handle for a cached derived key. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The destructor zeroes the key bytes in memory before releasing them, ensuring key material does not linger on the heap.</para>
<para>Raw key bytes are never exposed through the public interface. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
